Fixed G2: MSSQL availability groups
fetch `dt.entity.sql:sql_server_availability_group`
| fields id, tags
| expand tag = tags
| filter startsWith(tag, "Instance_Name:MSSQLSERVER@")
| fieldsAdd hostShort = lower(splitString(tag, "@")[1])
| lookup [
    fetch dt.entity.host
    | fields hostName = entity.name, tags
    | expand t = tags
    | filter startsWith(t, "APMID:")
    | fieldsAdd apmid = splitString(t, "APMID:")[1],
                hostShort = lower(splitString(hostName, ".")[0])
    | filter in(apmid, array($ClaimsApps))
    | summarize claimsApps = collectDistinct(apmid), hostRows = count(), by:{hostShort}
  ], sourceField: hostShort, lookupField: hostShort, prefix: "h."
| summarize agsTotal         = countDistinctExact(id),
            agsMatchedToHost = countDistinctExact(if(isNotNull(h.hostRows), id))


I pre-filtered the lookup to Claims apps, so agsMatchedToHost is the number of availability groups on a Claims host. If agsTotal is much larger, most availability groups don't belong to Claims.

New checks

H1: PostgreSQL instances on Claims hosts

timeseries up = avg(postgres.uptime, scalar: true), by:{device.name, device}, from:-2h
| fieldsAdd hostShort = lower(splitString(device.name, ".")[0])
| lookup [
    fetch dt.entity.host
    | fields hostName = entity.name, tags
    | expand t = tags
    | filter startsWith(t, "APMID:")
    | fieldsAdd apmid = splitString(t, "APMID:")[1],
                hostShort = lower(splitString(hostName, ".")[0])
    | filter in(apmid, array($ClaimsApps))
    | summarize claimsApps = collectDistinct(apmid), by:{hostShort}
  ], sourceField: hostShort, lookupField: hostShort, prefix: "h."
| summarize pgInstances   = count(),
            onClaimsHosts = countIf(isNotNull(h.claimsApps)),
            claimsApps    = countDistinctExact(h.claimsApps)


If onClaimsHosts is high, PostgreSQL health can be linked to apps through the host. To list the rows, replace the last summarize with | fields device, up, h.claimsApps | sort device asc.

H2: Do the z/OS DB2 processes carry Claims APMIDs?

timeseries fails = sum(dt.process.zos.db2.num_failed_connections, scalar: true),
           by:{dt.entity.process_group_instance}, from:-2h
| lookup [
    fetch dt.entity.process_group_instance
    | fields id, pgiName = entity.name, tags
    | expand t = tags
    | filter startsWith(t, "APMID:")
    | fieldsAdd apmid = splitString(t, "APMID:")[1]
  ], sourceField: dt.entity.process_group_instance, lookupField: id, prefix: "p."
| summarize pgisWithApmid = countDistinctExact(dt.entity.process_group_instance),
            claimsPgis    = countDistinctExact(if(in(p.apmid, array($ClaimsApps)), dt.entity.process_group_instance)),
            claimsApps    = countDistinctExact(if(in(p.apmid, array($ClaimsApps)), p.apmid))
